module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.AffineLocalizationTriangle
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.SectionsIso.HomologyComparison
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.LowDegree.LocalizationData
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The low-degree exact sequence for a finitely generated ideal

Let `A` be a commutative ring, `I ⊆ A` a finitely generated ideal, `U = Spec A \ V(I)` and `M` an
`A`-module. `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/LocalCohomology/LowDegree/ExactSequence.lean` deduces the
four-term sequence

`0 ⟶ H⁰_{V(I)}(M) ⟶ M ⟶ Γ(U, F) ⟶ H¹_{V(I)}(M) ⟶ 0`

from a `Stacks.LocalCohomology.LocalizationTriangleData`, and
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/LocalCohomology/AffineLocalizationTriangle.lean` supplies its left-hand
injectivity unconditionally. This file constructs the data, so that the sequence is no longer
conditional.

The construction is the composite of the two reductions already available. Choosing generators
`I = (f₁, …, f_r)`, `Stacks.LocalCohomology.localizationTriangleDataOfCechHomologyComparison`
reduces the data to two statements about the comparison of the degree-zero cohomology of the Čech
cone with the degree-one Čech cocycles — naturality in the module and the formula `m ↦ (m / 1)ᵢ` —
and `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/LocalCohomology/SectionsIso/HomologyComparison.lean` proves both. Any
finitely generated ideal admits a finite family of generators indexed by `Fin r`, so the data
exists for every finitely generated ideal.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_localizationTriangleData'` — a finitely generated ideal admits
  the localization triangle data.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_lowDegreeLocalizationExactSequence` — **the four-term exact
  sequence `0 ⟶ H⁰_{V(I)}(M) ⟶ M ⟶ Γ(U, F) ⟶ H¹_{V(I)}(M) ⟶ 0`**, with the middle map given by
  `m ↦ m / 1`.

## Implementation notes

This is Stacks 0DWR in degrees `0` and `1` only, so the tag is not attached here. Tag 0DWR also
asserts the isomorphisms `H^p(U, F) ≅ H^{p+1}_{V(I)}(M)` for `p ≥ 1`, which would need the third
term of the localization triangle to be identified with `RΓ(U, F)` in every degree and not only in
degree zero, and the statement that for `M = Γ(U, F)` both `H⁰_{V(I)}(M)` and `H¹_{V(I)}(M)`
vanish. The same four-term sequence is clause (2) of Stacks 0BK0 in degrees `0` and `1`; the
Noetherian hypothesis on `A` and the coherence of `F` that 0BK0 carries are not used.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DWR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DWR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BK0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BK0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A6Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A6Q)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe v u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (I : Ideal R) (hI : I.FG)

variable {I}

/-- A finitely generated ideal is generated by a family indexed by a `Fin r`. -/
theorem exists_fin_span_range (hI : I.FG) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → R), Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hI
  refine ⟨s.card, fun i => (s.equivFin.symm i : R), ?_⟩
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg Ideal.span ?_) hs
  ext x
  simp only [Set.mem_range, Finset.mem_coe]
  exact ⟨fun ⟨i, hi⟩ => hi ▸ (s.equivFin.symm i).2, fun hx => ⟨s.equivFin ⟨x, hx⟩, by simp⟩⟩

/-- **A finitely generated ideal admits the localization triangle data.** Choosing a finite family
of generators of `I` and applying
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechLocalizationTriangleData` removes the choice of generators from the
statement.

The module universe here is `max u v`;
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_localizationTriangleData` has it independent of the ring
universe. -/
theorem nonempty_localizationTriangleData' (hI : I.FG) :
    Nonempty (LocalizationTriangleData.{u, max u v} R I hI) :=
  have ⟨_, f, hf⟩ := exists_fin_span_range hI
  ⟨cechLocalizationTriangleData.{v} f I hI hf⟩

/-- **The low-degree localization exact sequence.** Let `I` be a finitely generated ideal of a
commutative ring `R`, let `U = Spec R \ V(I)`, let `M` be an `R`-module and let `F` be a sheaf of
modules on `U` identified with the restriction of the quasi-coherent module `M̃` generated by `M`.
Then there are an `R`-linear restriction map `M ⟶ Γ(U, F)` sending `m` to the section `m / 1` and
an `R`-linear connecting map `Γ(U, F) ⟶ H¹_{V(I)}(M)` which make

`0 ⟶ H⁰_{V(I)}(M) ⟶ M ⟶ Γ(U, F) ⟶ H¹_{V(I)}(M) ⟶ 0`

exact: the canonical map `H⁰_{V(I)}(M) ⟶ M` is injective, the sequence is exact at `M` and at
`Γ(U, F)`, and the connecting map is surjective.

This is Stacks 0DWR in degrees `0` and `1`, and clause (2) of Stacks 0BK0 in degrees `0` and `1`:
the Noetherian hypothesis and the coherence of `F` that 0BK0 carries are not needed. -/
@[ega "III 1.4.3" "(1.4.3.2), special case", sga "2 II Corollary4" "partial"]
theorem exists_lowDegreeLocalizationExactSequence (hI : I.FG) (M : ModuleCat.{max u v} R)
    (F : SheafOfModules.{max u v} (complementZeroLocus R I : Scheme).ringCatSheaf)
    (e : F ≅ complementTilde R I M) :
    ∃ (res : M →ₗ[R] complementGlobalSections R I F)
      (bd : complementGlobalSections R I F →ₗ[R] localCohomologyModule R I hI M 1),
      (∀ m : M, res m = e.inv.val.app (op ⊤)
          ⟨fun x ↦ LocalizedModule.mk m (1 : x.1.asIdeal.primeCompl),
            fun x ↦ ⟨_, x.2, 𝟙 _, m, 1, fun y ↦ ⟨by simp [Ideal.IsPrime.one_notMem], rfl⟩⟩⟩) ∧
        Function.Injective (localCohomologyZeroToModule R I hI M).hom ∧
        Function.Exact (localCohomologyZeroToModule R I hI M) res ∧
        Function.Exact res bd ∧ Function.Surjective bd :=
  have ⟨D⟩ := nonempty_localizationTriangleData'.{v} hI
  ⟨restrictionToComplement D M F e, localizationBoundary D M F e,
    restrictionToComplement_apply D M F e,
    localCohomologyZeroToModule_injective R I hI M,
    exact_localCohomologyZeroToModule_restrictionToComplement D M F e,
    exact_restrictionToComplement_localizationBoundary D M F e,
    localizationBoundary_surjective D M F e⟩

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

end
